{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Step modes over step (flow step debugger P2): drive(state, mode, pick, target, budget) -> {status, mode, stopped, steps, ended, depth, ready, default, event, events, state}. mode: into = one step; over = one step, and if it opened a unit (pushed a frame, started a list/loop op, or began an iteration) continue until that unit closed (a frame: its leave AND the enclosing op's closing eval); out = finish the innermost open unit (the op in progress in the top frame; else the top nested frame through its enclosing op's closing eval; in the root with nothing in progress, to the end); run_to = continue until the next DEFAULT pick is target {kind: wire|sync|op, index} (optional frame path [[op,iter],...] and case) - a breakpoint, it stops BEFORE the item runs; continue = to the end. The first step uses pick ({} = default; a not-ready pick is refused with the state unchanged), later steps the default pick, so over == into followed by out. budget bounds the steps (<=0 means 10000; stopped = budget is a pause, not an event). stopped: stepped | reached | ended | budget. Pass target {} when the mode does not use it.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"state","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"mode","type":"String"},{"name":"pick","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"target","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"budget","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"iijpnu1a16a2cc451mc1","readers":[],"time":1792782748764,"username":"system","writers":[]}